WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:17.808
On Monday morning, Katie's accident was big news in Ms. Barrow's classroom.

2
00:00:17.809 --> 00:00:24.825
"The next thing I knew, she was falling through the air!" said Joy to the fourth graders.

3
00:00:24.826 --> 00:00:28.411
"Did she scream?" asked Laura.

4
00:00:28.412 --> 00:00:31.441
Joy looked at Olivia. "I don't remember.

5
00:00:31.442 --> 00:00:33.206
Did she scream?"

6
00:00:33.207 --> 00:00:38.413
"No, she didn't," said Olivia. "She didn't even cry."

7
00:00:38.414 --> 00:00:44.124
"Dad picked her up, and Mom drove them to Dr. Howarth's office," said Joy.

8
00:00:44.125 --> 00:00:47.790
"Did she break her leg?" asked Larry.

9
00:00:47.791 --> 00:00:51.146
"No, she twisted her ankle," said Joy.

10
00:00:51.147 --> 00:00:54.568
"She has a bandage from her toes almost to her knee.

11
00:00:54.569 --> 00:00:57.527
And she has to put ice on her ankle."

12
00:00:57.528 --> 00:01:03.036
"And she doesn't have to come to school for at least two days," said Olivia.

13
00:01:03.037 --> 00:01:04.964
She looked at Ms. Barrow.

14
00:01:04.965 --> 00:01:08.523
"I mean she doesn't get to come to school.

15
00:01:08.524 --> 00:01:13.275
She has to rest."

16
00:01:13.276 --> 00:01:19.346
"Did you fill up your cart with walnuts yesterday?" Ms. Barrow asked Joy.

17
00:01:19.347 --> 00:01:23.525
"Yes, I did. Then Dad and I took them to the nut-buying station.

18
00:01:23.526 --> 00:01:27.154
We had to—before the price dropped!"

19
00:01:27.155 --> 00:01:33.453
Then Joy explained about the price falling from fifteen cents to thirteen cents.

20
00:01:33.454 --> 00:01:39.631
"Just when I had my money goal all figured out, the price changed," said Joy.

21
00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:44.114
"That doesn't seem fair." She sighed.

22
00:01:44.115 --> 00:01:47.193
"Mr. Ramirez at the nut-buying station—"

23
00:01:47.194 --> 00:01:50.723
"That's my dad," said Carlos.

24
00:01:50.724 --> 00:01:56.919
Joy continued. "Mr. Ramirez said the price dropped because there are so many walnuts this year.

25
00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:59.637
But I still don't understand it."

26
00:01:59.638 --> 00:02:02.976
"I'll try to explain," said Ms. Barrow.

27
00:02:02.977 --> 00:02:09.722
"You see, as Carlos's father said, there are a lot of walnuts this year.

28
00:02:09.723 --> 00:02:15.110
And the nut company knows there are plenty of nuts to keep their plant operating.

29
00:02:15.111 --> 00:02:19.075
But there are more nuts than people want.

30
00:02:19.076 --> 00:02:27.770
An increase in the supply—of cars or houses or anything—always causes the price to go down."

31
00:02:27.771 --> 00:02:29.801
Joy thought for a moment.

32
00:02:29.802 --> 00:02:36.666
"In other years, when there aren't so many walnuts, will the nut company pay more?" she asked.

33
00:02:36.667 --> 00:02:39.133
"Yes," said Ms. Barrow.

34
00:02:39.134 --> 00:02:45.375
"They'll pay more for walnuts so people will work harder and collect more."

35
00:02:45.376 --> 00:02:49.370
"Are you close to your goal?" Larry asked Joy.

36
00:02:49.371 --> 00:02:52.338
Joy opened her little notebook.

37
00:02:52.339 --> 00:02:56.108
"On Saturday, I made twenty-five dollars and fifty cents.

38
00:02:56.109 --> 00:03:00.936
On Sunday, I made twenty-four dollars and forty-five cents."

39
00:03:00.937 --> 00:03:09.444
"How much more does Joy need to reach her goal of one hundred dollars?" asked Ms. Barrow.

40
00:03:09.445 --> 00:03:14.003
The fourth graders worked on the problem. "How much, Luke?"

41
00:03:14.004 --> 00:03:18.456
"Fifty dollars and five cents," answered Luke.

42
00:03:18.457 --> 00:03:21.415
"That is exactly right," said Joy.

43
00:03:21.416 --> 00:03:26.642
"And that means I have to collect 385 more pounds of walnuts.

44
00:03:26.643 --> 00:03:29.461
Then I can fix my fiddle."

45
00:03:29.462 --> 00:03:33.500
After school that day, Olivia visited Katie.

46
00:03:33.501 --> 00:03:36.586
She sat on Joy's bed, across from Katie.

47
00:03:36.587 --> 00:03:40.058
"See my bandage?" said Katie.

48
00:03:40.059 --> 00:03:41.820
"And my ice pack?

49
00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:44.573
I have to keep my ankle elevated.

50
00:03:44.574 --> 00:03:49.138
That means I have to prop it up on these pillows."

51
00:03:49.139 --> 00:03:52.211
"Does it hurt?" asked Olivia.

52
00:03:52.212 --> 00:03:54.935
"A little bit," said Katie.

53
00:03:54.936 --> 00:03:59.990
"But the worst part is that I can't help Joy with her goal anymore."

54
00:03:59.991 --> 00:04:02.914
"What about the hayride?" said Olivia.

55
00:04:02.915 --> 00:04:05.441
"Will you be able to go?"

56
00:04:05.442 --> 00:04:11.547
"The hayride!" said Katie and hit her forehead with her hand.

57
00:04:11.548 --> 00:04:13.376
"I almost forgot!

58
00:04:13.377 --> 00:04:16.529
Can you bring me the calendar on my desk, please?

59
00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:18.722
What day is today?"

60
00:04:18.723 --> 00:04:21.983
"Monday," said Olivia.

61
00:04:21.984 --> 00:04:26.963
"I've got less than two weeks to get well," said Katie.

62
00:04:26.964 --> 00:04:30.363
She thought for a moment and then sighed.

63
00:04:30.364 --> 00:04:34.076
"But Joy has only one more weekend to collect nuts.

64
00:04:34.077 --> 00:04:37.120
And she's lost her helper."

65
00:04:37.121 --> 00:04:40.082
Joy's fiddle was lying on Joy's desk.

66
00:04:40.083 --> 00:04:43.255
Olivia touched the broken strings.

67
00:04:43.256 --> 00:04:45.829
Then she looked at Katie.

68
00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:51.051
"I have an idea," she said. "I'll be her helper!

69
00:04:51.052 --> 00:04:56.799
I'll come here Saturday morning and help Joy collect walnuts!"
